abstract:
Let $\Omega\subset {\mathbb C}^n$ be a bounded domain with the hyperconvexity index $\alpha(\Omega)>0$. Let $\varrho$ be the relative extremal function of a fixed closed ball in $\Omega$ and set $\mu:=|\varrho|(1+|\log|\varrho||)^{-1}$, $
u:=|\varrho|(1+|\log|\varrho||)^n$. We obtain the following estimates for the Bergman kernel: (1) For every $0<\alpha<\alpha(\Omega)$ and $2\le p<2+ rac{2\alpha(\Omega)}{2n-\alpha(\Omega)}$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that $\int_\Omega | rac{K_\Omega(\cdot,w)}{\sqrt{K_\Omega(w)}}|^{p}\le C |\mu(w)|^{- rac{(p-2) n}\alpha}$ for all $w\in \Omega$. (2) For every $0<r<1$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that $  rac{|K_\Omega(z,w)|^2}{K_\Omega(z)K_\Omega(w)}\le C (\min\{ rac{
u(z)}{\mu(w)}, rac{
u(w)}{\mu(z)}\})^r $ for all $z,w\in \Omega$. Various application of these estimates are given.

Let $\mathfrak{g}$ be a simple, finite-dimensional Lie (super)algebra equipped with an embedding of $\mathfrak{s} \mathfrak{l}_2$ inducing the minimal gradation on $\mathfrak{g}$. The corresponding minimal $\mathcal{W}$-algebra $\mathcal{W}^k(\mathfrak{g}, e_{-	heta})$ introduced by Kac and Wakimoto has strong generators in weights $1,2,3/2$, and all operator product expansions are known explicitly. The weight one subspace generates an affine vertex (super)algebra $V^{k'}(\mathfrak{g}^{
atural})$ where $\mathfrak{g}^{
atural} \subset \mathfrak{g}$ denotes the centralizer of $\mathfrak{s} \mathfrak{l}_2$. Therefore $\mathcal{W}^k(\mathfrak{g}, e_{-	heta})$ has an action of a connected Lie group $G^{
atural}_0$ with Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}^{
atural}_0$, where $\mathfrak{g}^{
atural}_0$ denotes the even part of $\mathfrak{g}^{
atural}$. We show that for any reductive subgroup $G \subset G^{
atural}_0$, and for any reductive Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}' \subset \mathfrak{g}^{
atural}$, the orbifold $\mathcal{O}^k = \mathcal{W}^k(\mathfrak{g}, e_{-	heta})^{G}$ and the coset $\mathcal{C}^k = 	ext{Com}(V(\mathfrak{g}'),\mathcal{W}^k(\mathfrak{g}, e_{-	heta}))$ are strongly finitely generated for generic values of $k$. Here $V(\mathfrak{g}')$ denotes the affine vertex algebra associated to $\mathfrak{g}'$. We find explicit minimal strong generating sets for $\mathcal{C}^k$ when $\mathfrak{g}' = \mathfrak{g}^{
atural}$ and $\mathfrak{g}$ is either $\mathfrak{s} \mathfrak{l}_n$, $\mathfrak{s}\mathfrak{p}_{2n}$, $\mathfrak{s}\mathfrak{l}(2|n)$ for $n
eq 2$, $\mathfrak{p}\mathfrak{s}\mathfrak{l}(2|2)$, or $\mathfrak{o}\mathfrak{s}\mathfrak{p}(1|4)$. Finally, we conjecture some surprising coincidences among families of cosets $\mathcal{C}_k$ which are the simple quotients of $\mathcal{C}^k$, and we prove several cases of our conjecture.
